{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AfUfM8SNXHdwJV5R5JBATC","type":"tool_result","content":" 21:44:48 up 13 days,  9:49,  1 user,  load average: 0.13, 0.49, 0.78\n== covers: the 600 certified (6, 1) instances with Harper on record ==\ncovers: 600 instances in 58 s wall (0.10 core-hours of bounds; Harper read from the record)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c821cc2c-f627-4785-bc52-942e492e87f6","uuid":"04875aca-1ae7-4dfb-b571-538ffa141303","timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:45:47.267Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":" 21:44:48 up 13 days,  9:49,  1 user,  load average: 0.13, 0.49, 0.78\n== covers: the 600 certified (6, 1) instances with Harper on record ==\ncovers: 600 instances in 58 s wall (0.10 core-hours of bounds; Harper read from the record)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":true,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger/run.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":372,"lines":["+\"\"\"loop0011 item 11: the slack ledger — in stacks, what each count buys and what","+is left, on certified instances (`reports/separator_moment.md` §11).","+","+Every quantity is on the *pathwidth* scale (`pw = optimum − 1` on covers; the","+proved width on the pilot graphs).  A floor at threshold `θ` is the largest `k`","+with the count's bound on `P(pw ≤ k)` below `θ`, plus one (`learning.","+separator_moment.floor_pw`; the record's `floors` is this plus one more, for","+the optimum).  The ladder per instance is","+","+    old pair → exact-size pair → {closed, flip | separator, closed} → Harper → pw,","+","+where `Harper` is the vertex-isoperimetric bound under a level cap and a time","+budget (a *lower* bound on the true Harper value, which is itself ≤ pw), so","+`pw − Harper` is an *upper* bound on the necessary condition's slack and","+`Harper − floor` a *lower* bound on the union bound's (§8.5 (b) of","+`reports/excess_phase_diagram.md`).","+","+Stages (`--stage covers|gnp|stats|draw`, all by default):","+  covers  the 600 certified `(6, 1)` fixed-generator instances at `n = m = 30–75`","+          whose Harper values are on record (`reports/scratch/structured_count/","+          slack_6_1.csv`, read, never re-solved): sizes regenerated from the","+          seeds (`learning.ensemble.generate`), the old pair floor, the","+          exact-size pair floor, the closed-pair floor (NA bound, item 07) and the","+          flip floor (item 07), at `< 1` and `< 0.01`.","+  gnp     the pilot's `c = 10` cells at `n = 30, 40, 50, 60` (`reports/scratch/","+          gnp_pilot/results.csv`, proved graphs only, regenerated from their","+          seeds; the layout re-checked against the width): per cell the old and","+          exact-size pair floors, the separator floor (item 05: `C(n, k)","+          P_N(E_bip)`, exact) and the closed floor (item 06: `log_closed_count`);","+          per graph Harper's bound (`harper_bound_graph`, `--max-t` levels,","+          `--budget` seconds, censoring recorded).","+  stats   per `n`, the quantiles of every consecutive difference of the ladder,","+          the violation counts (a floor above `pw` at `< 0.01` is the stop","+          condition of TASK.md), and where the slack sits.","+  draw    the ladder figure (medians per `n`, gap to `pw`), PNG.","+","+Outputs here: ledger_6_1.csv, ledger_gnp.csv, cells_gnp.csv, summary.csv,","+ladder.png, run.log.","+","+Regenerate: nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger/run.py --workers 6","+\"\"\"","+from __future__ import annotations","+","+import argparse","+import csv","+import math","+import os","+import sys","+import time","+from multiprocessing import Pool","+","+import numpy as np","+","+ROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\", \"..\", \"..\"))","+HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))","+sys.path.insert(0, ROOT)","+os.chdir(ROOT)","+","+from learning import separator_moment as sm  # noqa: E402","+from learning.first_moment import floors as pair_floors, log_bound, lchoose  # noqa: E402","+","+LN10 = math.log(10)","+SLACK = \"reports/scratch/structured_count/slack_6_1.csv\"","+PILOT = \"reports/scratch/gnp_pilot/results.csv\"","+THRESH = {\"lt1\": 1.0, \"lt001\": 0.01}","+","+","+def log(msg: str = \"\") -> None:","+    print(msg, flush=True)","+    with open(os.path.join(HERE, \"run.log\"), \"a\") as f:","+        f.write(msg + \"\\n\")","+","+","+def write_csv(path: str, rows: list[dict]) -> None:","+    with open(path, \"w\", newline=\"\") as f:","+        w = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=list(rows[0].keys()))","+        w.writeheader()","+        w.writerows(rows)","+","+","+def read_csv(path: str) -> list[dict]:","+    with open(path) as f:","+        return list(csv.DictReader(f))","+","+","+# ------------------------------------------------------------------ covers","+","+def cover_task(args):","+    frame, cell_text, index, name, rec = args","+    from learning.ensemble import Cell, generate","+    t0 = time.time()","+    inst = generate(Cell(cell_text[0], cell_text[1], cell_text[2], cell_text[3]), index)","+    assert inst.name == name, (inst.name, name)","+    sizes = [int(s) for s in np.asarray(inst.matrix).sum(axis=0)]","+    n = inst.n_customers","+    assert n == int(rec[\"n\"]) and inst.n_patterns == int(rec[\"m\"])","+    pw = int(rec[\"optimum\"]) - 1","+    old = {k: log_bound(n, sizes, k) for k in range(n)}","+    xp = {k: sm.cover_log_pair_bound(n, k, sizes) for k in range(n)}","+    o1, o2 = sm.floor_pw(old, 1.0), sm.floor_pw(old, 0.01)","+    x1, x2 = sm.floor_pw(xp, 1.0), sm.floor_pw(xp, 0.01)","+    # the record's floors (optimum scale) must be these plus one","+    f_old = pair_floors(n, sizes)","+    assert (o1 + 1, o2 + 1) == f_old == (int(rec[\"floor_old\"]), int(rec[\"floor_old_001\"])), (name, o1, o2, f_old, rec)","+    assert (x1 + 1, x2 + 1) == (int(rec[\"floor_1\"]), int(rec[\"floor_1_001\"])), (name, x1, x2, rec)","+    # closed and flip around the exact-size floors (each k is its own statement; the window holds the floors)","+    ks = list(range(max(0, x2 - 5), min(n - 1, max(x1 + 7, pw + 1)) + 1))","+    cl = {k: sm.closed_cover_log_bound(n, k, sizes, optimise=False) for k in ks}","+    fl = {k: sm.flip_log_bound_fast(n, k, sizes)[0] for k in ks}","+    c1, c2 = sm.floor_pw(cl, 1.0), sm.floor_pw(cl, 0.01)","+    f1, f2 = sm.floor_pw(fl, 1.0), sm.floor_pw(fl, 0.01)","+    harper = int(rec[\"harper\"]) - 1          # the record's value is on the MOSP scale","+    return {\"frame\": frame, \"instance\": name, \"n\": n, \"m\": inst.n_patterns, \"pw\": pw,","+            \"old_lt1\": o1, \"xpair_lt1\": x1, \"closed_lt1\": c1, \"flip_lt1\": f1,","+            \"old_lt001\": o2, \"xpair_lt001\": x2, \"closed_lt001\": c2, \"flip_lt001\": f2,","+            \"best_lt1\": max(c1, f1, x1), \"best_lt001\": max(c2, f2, x2),","+            \"harper\": harper, \"harper_cap\": int(rec[\"cap\"]), \"harper_complete\": rec[\"complete\"] == \"True\",","+            \"harper_secs\": round(float(rec[\"secs\"]), 1),","+            \"log10_old_at_pw\": old[pw] / LN10, \"log10_xpair_at_pw\": xp[pw] / LN10,","+            \"log10_closed_at_pw\": cl.get(pw, float(\"nan\")) / LN10, \"log10_flip_at_pw\": fl.get(pw, float(\"nan\")) / LN10,","+            \"k_scanned\": f\"{ks[0]}-{ks[-1]}\", \"seconds\": round(time.time() - t0, 2)}","+","+","+def stage_covers(workers: int) -> None:","+    import pandas as pd","+    log(\"== covers: the 600 certified (6, 1) instances with Harper on record ==\")","+    t0 = time.time()","+    rec = {r[\"instance\"]: r for r in read_csv(SLACK)}","+    tasks = []","+    for frame in (\"results.csv\", \"results_upward.csv\"):","+        df = pd.read_csv(f\"learning/data/ensemble/{frame}\")","+        sub = df[(df.generator == \"fixed\") & (df.param == 6) & (df.m == df.n) & (df.n >= 30)]","+        assert sub.certified.all()","+        for r in sub.itertuples():","+            assert r.instance_name in rec and int(rec[r.instance_name][\"optimum\"]) == int(r.optimum)","+            tasks.append((frame, (r.generator, int(r.n), int(r.m), float(r.param)), int(r.index), r.instance_name, rec[r.instance_name]))","+    assert len(tasks) == len(rec) == 600, (len(tasks), len(rec))","+    tasks.sort(key=lambda t: -t[1][1])","+    with Pool(workers) as pool:","+        rows = pool.map(cover_task, tasks, chunksize=2)","+    rows.sort(key=lambda r: (r[\"n\"], r[\"instance\"]))","+    write_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \"ledger_6_1.csv\"), rows)","+    log(f\"covers: {len(rows)} instances in {time.time() - t0:.0f} s wall ({sum(r['seconds'] for r in rows) / 3600:.2f} core-hours of bounds; Harper read from the record)\")","+","+","+# ------------------------------------------------------------------ gnp","+","+def cell_task(args):","+    n, c = args","+    p = c / n","+    t0 = time.time()","+    lc = sm.log_connected(n, p)","+    rows = []","+    for k in range(n):","+        N, t = sm.forced_sizes(n, k)","+        lck = lchoose(n, k)","+        rows.append({\"n\": n, \"c\": c, \"k\": k, \"N\": N, \"t\": t,","+                     \"logB_old\": lchoose(n, t) + lchoose(n - t, t - 1) + t * (t - 1) * math.log1p(-p) if t >= 1 else math.inf,","+                     \"logB_xpair\": lck + sm.log_product_bound(N, p, t),","+                     \"logB_sep\": lck + sm.log_prob_bip(N, p, t, lc),","+                     \"logB_closed\": sm.log_closed_count(n, k, p)})","+    return n, c, rows, time.time() - t0","+","+","+def harper_task(args):","+    n, c, sample, seed, width, m, max_t, budget = args","+    adj = sm.gnp_masks(n, c / n, seed)","+    assert sum(popc(a) for a in adj) // 2 == m, (n, c, seed)","+    hb = sm.harper_bound_graph(adj, max_t=max_t, time_budget=budget)","+    return {\"n\": n, \"c\": c, \"sample\": sample, \"seed\": seed, \"pw\": width, \"harper\": hb.value, \"harper_cap\": hb.cap,","+            \"harper_levels\": \" \".join(map(str, hb.levels)), \"harper_complete\": hb.complete, \"harper_secs\": round(hb.seconds, 1)}","+","+","+def popc(x: int) -> int:","+    return bin(x).count(\"1\")","+","+","+def stage_gnp(workers: int, max_t: int, budget: float) -> None:","+    log(f\"== gnp: the pilot's c = 10 cells at n = 30–60, proved graphs; Harper with max_t {max_t}, budget {budget:.0f} s ==\")","+    t0 = time.time()","+    pilot = [r for r in read_csv(PILOT) if float(r[\"c\"]) == 10 and int(r[\"n\"]) in (30, 40, 50, 60)]","+    proved = [r for r in pilot if r[\"status\"] != \"upper\"]","+    for r in proved:","+        assert int(r[\"lower\"]) == int(r[\"width\"]), r","+    log(f\"  {len(pilot)} graphs in the four cells, {len(proved)} proved ({sum(1 for r in pilot if r['status'] == 'minor')} by a minor certificate)\")","+    # the layout on record has the width (both orientations tried: the C program's convention is not pinned here)","+    bad = 0","+    for r in proved:","+        n = int(r[\"n\"])","+        adj = sm.gnp_masks(n, 10 / n, int(r[\"seed\"]))","+        lay = [int(x) for x in r[\"layout\"].split()]","+        vs = min(sm.layout_vertex_separation(adj, lay), sm.layout_vertex_separation(adj, lay[::-1]))","+        if vs != int(r[\"width\"]):","+            bad += 1","+    log(f\"  layout check: {len(proved) - bad} of {len(proved)} layouts have the recorded width in one orientation, {bad} do not\")","+    with Pool(workers) as pool:","+        cells = pool.map(cell_task, [(n, 10) for n in (30, 40, 50, 60)])","+    cell_rows = []","+    for n, c, rows, secs in cells:","+        cell_rows.extend(rows)","+    write_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \"cells_gnp.csv\"), cell_rows)","+    log(f\"  cell bounds: {len(cell_rows)} (n, k) rows in {sum(s for *_, s in cells):.0f} s\")","+    tasks = [(int(r[\"n\"]), 10, int(r[\"sample\"]), int(r[\"seed\"]), int(r[\"width\"]), int(r[\"m\"]), max_t, budget) for r in proved]","+    tasks.sort(key=lambda t: -t[0])","+    with Pool(workers) as pool:","+        rows = pool.map(harper_task, tasks, chunksize=1)","+    by_cell = {}","+    for r in cell_rows:","+        by_cell.setdefault(int(r[\"n\"]), {})[int(r[\"k\"])] = r","+    for r in rows:","+        kb = by_cell[r[\"n\"]]","+        for key, lab in ((\"logB_old\", \"old\"), (\"logB_xpair\", \"xpair\"), (\"logB_sep\", \"sep\"), (\"logB_closed\", \"closed\")):","+            vals = {k: float(v[key]) for k, v in kb.items()}","+            r[f\"{lab}_lt1\"] = sm.floor_pw(vals, 1.0)","+            r[f\"{lab}_lt001\"] = sm.floor_pw(vals, 0.01)","+            r[f\"log10_{lab}_at_pw\"] = vals[r[\"pw\"]] / LN10","+        r[\"best_lt1\"] = max(r[\"sep_lt1\"], r[\"closed_lt1\"], r[\"xpair_lt1\"])","+        r[\"best_lt001\"] = max(r[\"sep_lt001\"], r[\"closed_lt001\"], r[\"xpair_lt001\"])","+    rows.sort(key=lambda r: (r[\"n\"], r[\"sample\"]))","+    write_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \"ledger_gnp.csv\"), rows)","+    log(f\"gnp: {len(rows)} graphs in {time.time() - t0:.0f} s wall ({sum(r['harper_secs'] for r in rows) / 3600:.2f} core-hours of Harper)\")","+","+","+# ------------------------------------------------------------------ stats","+","+def q(vals, ps=(10, 50, 90)):","+    return \" / \".join(f\"{np.percentile(vals, p):.0f}\" for p in ps)","+","+","+def ledger_stats(rows: list[dict], model: str, counts: list[tuple[str, str]], thr: str) -> list[dict]:","+    \"\"\"Per `n`: quantiles and means of the consecutive differences at threshold `thr`.\"\"\"","+    out = []","+    ns = sorted({int(r[\"n\"]) for r in rows})","+    log(f\"\\n{model}, floors at < {THRESH[thr]} (pw scale; quantiles 10 / 50 / 90, mean in brackets)\")","+    header = \"  n   N | \" + \" | \".join(f\"{b}−{a}\" for a, b in counts) + \" | Harper−best | pw−Harper | pw−best | share union-bound | Harper≥best | Harper=pw | viol\"","+    log(header)","+    for n in ns:","+        g = [r for r in rows if int(r[\"n\"]) == n]","+        pw = np.array([int(r[\"pw\"]) for r in g])","+        best = np.array([int(r[f\"best_{thr}\"]) for r in g])","+        harper = np.array([int(r[\"harper\"]) for r in g])","+        d = {\"model\": model, \"thresh\": THRESH[thr], \"n\": n, \"N\": len(g), \"mean_pw\": pw.mean(), \"mean_harper\": harper.mean()}","+        cells = []","+        for a, b in counts:","+            diff = np.array([int(r[f\"{b}_{thr}\"]) - int(r[f\"{a}_{thr}\"]) for r in g])","+            d[f\"{b}_minus_{a}_mean\"] = diff.mean()","+            d[f\"{b}_minus_{a}_q\"] = q(diff)","+            d[f\"mean_{a}\"] = np.mean([int(r[f\"{a}_{thr}\"]) for r in g])","+            d[f\"mean_{b}\"] = np.mean([int(r[f\"{b}_{thr}\"]) for r in g])","+            cells.append(f\"{q(diff)} ({diff.mean():.2f})\")","+        hb, ph, pb = harper - best, pw - harper, pw - best","+        share = hb.sum() / pb.sum() if pb.sum() else float(\"nan\")","+        d.update(harper_minus_best_mean=hb.mean(), harper_minus_best_q=q(hb), pw_minus_harper_mean=ph.mean(), pw_minus_harper_q=q(ph),","+                 pw_minus_best_mean=pb.mean(), pw_minus_best_q=q(pb), share_union_bound=share,","+                 harper_ge_best=int((hb >= 0).sum()), harper_eq_pw=int((ph == 0).sum()),","+                 violations=int((best > pw).sum()), mean_best=best.mean(),","+                 cap_min=min(int(r[\"harper_cap\"]) for r in g), cap_median=float(np.median([int(r[\"harper_cap\"]) for r in g])),","+                 complete=sum(1 for r in g if str(r[\"harper_complete\"]) == \"True\"),","+                 harper_secs_mean=float(np.mean([float(r[\"harper_secs\"]) for r in g])))","+        log(f\"{n:4d} {len(g):3d} | \" + \" | \".join(cells) + f\" | {q(hb)} ({hb.mean():.2f}) | {q(ph)} ({ph.mean():.2f}) | {q(pb)} ({pb.mean():.2f}) | {share:.2f} | {d['harper_ge_best']} | {d['harper_eq_pw']} | {d['violations']}\")","+        out.append(d)","+    return out","+","+","+def stage_stats() -> None:","+    log(\"\\n== stats ==\")","+    cov = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \"ledger_6_1.csv\"))","+    gnp = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \"ledger_gnp.csv\"))","+    summary = []","+    for thr in (\"lt001\", \"lt1\"):","+        summary += ledger_stats(cov, \"covers (6, 1), fixed generator, m = n\", [(\"old\", \"xpair\"), (\"xpair\", \"closed\"), (\"xpair\", \"flip\")], thr)","+        summary += ledger_stats(gnp, \"G(n, 10/n), pilot, proved\", [(\"old\", \"xpair\"), (\"xpair\", \"sep\"), (\"xpair\", \"closed\")], thr)","+    write_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \"summary.csv\"), summary)","+    # violations at both thresholds, every count","+    log(\"\\nviolations (floor > pw), by count and threshold:\")","+    for name, rows, keys in ((\"covers\", cov, (\"old\", \"xpair\", \"closed\", \"flip\")), (\"gnp\", gnp, (\"old\", \"xpair\", \"sep\", \"closed\"))):","+        for thr in (\"lt1\", \"lt001\"):","+            v = {k: sum(1 for r in rows if int(r[f\"{k}_{thr}\"]) > int(r[\"pw\"])) for k in keys}","+            log(f\"  {name} < {THRESH[thr]}: {v}\")","+    # Harper censoring","+    log(\"\\nHarper under the cap: covers (record, max_t 12, 60 s) and gnp (this item)\")","+    for name, rows in ((\"covers\", cov), (\"gnp\", gnp)):","+        for n in sorted({int(r[\"n\"]) for r in rows}):","+            g = [r for r in rows if int(r[\"n\"]) == n]","+            caps = [int(r[\"harper_cap\"]) for r in g]","+            t_forced = [math.ceil((int(r[\"n\"]) - int(r[\"pw\"])) / 2) for r in g]","+            log(f\"  {name} n={n}: cap min/median/max {min(caps)}/{np.median(caps):.0f}/{max(caps)}; forced t at pw: {min(t_forced)}–{max(t_forced)}; complete {sum(1 for r in g if str(r['harper_complete']) == 'True')}/{len(g)}; secs mean/max {np.mean([float(r['harper_secs']) for r in g]):.1f}/{max(float(r['harper_secs']) for r in g):.0f}\")","+    # per-cell floors on gnp (same for every graph in a cell) and the decades at pw","+    log(\"\\ngnp cells: floors (pw scale) at < 1 / < 0.01 and min/mean/max pw; log10 of each bound at k = min pw\")","+    cells = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \"cells_gnp.csv\"))","+    for n in (30, 40, 50, 60):","+        kb = {int(r[\"k\"]): r for r in cells if int(r[\"n\"]) == n}","+        g = [int(r[\"pw\"]) for r in gnp if int(r[\"n\"]) == n]","+        parts = []","+        for key, lab in ((\"logB_old\", \"old\"), (\"logB_xpair\", \"xpair\"), (\"logB_sep\", \"sep\"), (\"logB_closed\", \"closed\")):","+            vals = {k: float(v[key]) for k, v in kb.items()}","+            parts.append(f\"{lab} {sm.floor_pw(vals, 1.0)}/{sm.floor_pw(vals, 0.01)} ({vals[min(g)] / LN10:+.2f})\")","+        log(f\"  n={n}: \" + \"; \".join(parts) + f\"; pw {min(g)}/{np.mean(g):.1f}/{max(g)}\")","+    # the decades at k = pw on covers (mean per n)","+    log(\"\\ncovers: mean log10 of each count's bound at k = pw (the instance's own pathwidth)\")","+    for n in sorted({int(r[\"n\"]) for r in cov}):","+        g = [r for r in cov if int(r[\"n\"]) == n]","+        log(f\"  n={n}: old {np.mean([float(r['log10_old_at_pw']) for r in g]):+.2f}, xpair {np.mean([float(r['log10_xpair_at_pw']) for r in g]):+.2f}, \"","+            f\"closed {np.nanmean([float(r['log10_closed_at_pw']) for r in g]):+.2f}, flip {np.nanmean([float(r['log10_flip_at_pw']) for r in g]):+.2f}\")","+","+","+# ------------------------------------------------------------------ draw","+","+def stage_draw() -> None:","+    import matplotlib","+    matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")","+    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt","+    cov = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \"ledger_6_1.csv\"))","+    gnp = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \"ledger_gnp.csv\"))","+    # palette: reference categorical slots 1, 2, 3, 4 and text-primary for pw (validated, see run.log)","+    rungs_cov = [(\"old_lt001\", \"old pair floor\", \"#2a78d6\"), (\"xpair_lt001\", \"exact-size pair floor\", \"#eb6834\"),","+                 (\"best_lt001\", \"best count (closed / flip)\", \"#1baf7a\"), (\"harper\", \"Harper (capped)\", \"#eda100\"), (\"pw\", \"pathwidth\", \"#0b0b0b\")]","+    rungs_gnp = [(\"old_lt001\", \"old pair floor\", \"#2a78d6\"), (\"xpair_lt001\", \"exact-size pair floor\", \"#eb6834\"),","+                 (\"best_lt001\", \"best count (separator / closed)\", \"#1baf7a\"), (\"harper\", \"Harper (capped)\", \"#eda100\"), (\"pw\", \"pathwidth\", \"#0b0b0b\")]","+    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(10.5, 4.4), sharey=True)","+    for ax, rows, rungs, title in ((axes[0], cov, rungs_cov, \"random clique covers (6, 1), m = n, certified\"),","+                                   (axes[1], gnp, rungs_gnp, \"G(n, 10/n), pilot graphs, proved\")):","+        ns = sorted({int(r[\"n\"]) for r in rows})","+        for i, n in enumerate(ns):","+            g = [r for r in rows if int(r[\"n\"]) == n]","+            pw = np.array([int(r[\"pw\"]) for r in g])","+            meds = []","+            for key, lab, col in rungs:","+                gap = pw - np.array([int(r[key]) for r in g])","+                meds.append(float(np.median(gap)))","+            ax.plot([n, n], [max(meds), min(meds)], color=\"#c3c2b7\", linewidth=1.5, zorder=1)","+            for (key, lab, col), m in zip(rungs, meds):","+                ax.plot([n], [m], \"o\", color=col, markersize=8, markeredgecolor=\"#fcfcfb\", markeredgewidth=1.2, zorder=3,","+                        label=lab if i == 0 else None)","+                if i == len(ns) - 1:","+                    ax.annotate(lab, (n, m), xytext=(8, 0), textcoords=\"offset points\", fontsize=8, color=\"#52514e\", va=\"center\")","+        ax.set_xlabel(\"n\")","+        ax.set_title(title, fontsize=9, color=\"#52514e\", loc=\"left\")","+        ax.set_xticks(ns)","+        ax.set_xlim(min(ns) - 3, max(ns) + 22)","+        ax.grid(axis=\"y\", color=\"#e8e7e3\", linewidth=0.8)","+        for s in (\"top\", \"right\"):","+            ax.spines[s].set_visible(False)","+        ax.spines[\"left\"].set_color(\"#c3c2b7\")","+        ax.spines[\"bottom\"].set_color(\"#c3c2b7\")","+    axes[0].set_ylabel(\"stacks below the pathwidth (median per n)\")","+    axes[0].invert_yaxis()","+    axes[0].legend(loc=\"lower left\", fontsize=8, frameon=False)","+    fig.tight_layout()","+    fig.savefig(os.path.join(HERE, \"ladder.png\"), dpi=160)","+    log(\"draw: ladder.png\")","+","+","+def main() -> None:","+    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()","+    ap.add_argument(\"--stage\", default=\"all\", choices=[\"all\", \"covers\", \"gnp\", \"stats\", \"draw\"])","+    ap.add_argument(\"--workers\", type=int, default=6)","+    ap.add_argument(\"--max-t\", type=int, default=16)","+    ap.add_argument(\"--budget\", type=float, default=60.0)","+    a = ap.parse_args()","+    if a.stage in (\"all\", \"covers\"):","+        stage_covers(a.workers)","+    if a.stage in (\"all\", \"gnp\"):","+        stage_gnp(a.workers, a.max_t, a.budget)","+    if a.stage in (\"all\", \"stats\"):","+        stage_stats()","+    if a.stage in (\"all\", \"draw\"):","+        stage_draw()","+","+","+if __name__ == \"__main__\":","+    main()"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger/run.log","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":2,"lines":["+== covers: the 600 certified (6, 1) instances with Harper on record ==","+covers: 600 instances in 58 s wall (0.10 core-hours of bounds; Harper read from the record)"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/Ralph_Loops/loop0011/session_it11.jsonl","hunks":[{"oldStart":284,"oldLines":3,"newStart":284,"newLines":6,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5-1\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgcwLJDPiMEurKL2DJHFr\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":32,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1155,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":175245,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1155,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":4,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"c821cc2c-f627-4785-bc52-942e492e87f6\",\"uuid\":\"3400ea78-b62d-445d-9de4-4c0c64434842\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-01T21:43:13.825Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgcwLHn6aJM5Gd5VbCBX3\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":1806,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5-1\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgcwLJDPiMEurKL2DJHFr\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now the ledger script itself: stages `covers` (record Harper plus the four floors from regenerated sizes), `gnp` (per-cell bounds, per-graph Harper with a layout check), `stats` and `draw`.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":32,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1155,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":175245,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1155,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":4,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"c821cc2c-f627-4785-bc52-942e492e87f6\",\"uuid\":\"29ca5091-e8a8-48f0-93b1-0847e33c58d8\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-01T21:43:13.826Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgcwLHn6aJM5Gd5VbCBX3\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5-1\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgcwLJDPiMEurKL2DJHFr\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01AfUfM8SNXHdwJV5R5JBATC\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"mkdir -p reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger && cat > reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger/run.py <<'EOF'\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"loop0011 item 11: the slack ledger — in stacks, what each count buys and what\\nis left, on certified instances (`reports/separator_moment.md` §11).\\n\\nEvery quantity is on the *pathwidth* scale (`pw = optimum − 1` on covers; the\\nproved width on the pilot graphs).  A floor at threshold `θ` is the largest `k`\\nwith the count's bound on `P(pw ≤ k)` below `θ`, plus one (`learning.\\nseparator_moment.floor_pw`; the record's `floors` is this plus one more, for\\nthe optimum).  The ladder per instance is\\n\\n    old pair → exact-size pair → {closed, flip | separator, closed} → Harper → pw,\\n\\nwhere `Harper` is the vertex-isoperimetric bound under a level cap and a time\\nbudget (a *lower* bound on the true Harper value, which is itself ≤ pw), so\\n`pw − Harper` is an *upper* bound on the necessary condition's slack and\\n`Harper − floor` a *lower* bound on the union bound's (§8.5 (b) of\\n`reports/excess_phase_diagram.md`).\\n\\nStages (`--stage covers|gnp|stats|draw`, all by default):\\n  covers  the 600 certified `(6, 1)` fixed-generator instances at `n = m = 30–75`\\n          whose Harper values are on record (`reports/scratch/structured_count/\\n          slack_6_1.csv`, read, never re-solved): sizes regenerated from the\\n          seeds (`learning.ensemble.generate`), the old pair floor, the\\n          exact-size pair floor, the closed-pair floor (NA bound, item 07) and the\\n          flip floor (item 07), at `< 1` and `< 0.01`.\\n  gnp     the pilot's `c = 10` cells at `n = 30, 40, 50, 60` (`reports/scratch/\\n          gnp_pilot/results.csv`, proved graphs only, regenerated from their\\n          seeds; the layout re-checked against the width): per cell the old and\\n          exact-size pair floors, the separator floor (item 05: `C(n, k)\\n          P_N(E_bip)`, exact) and the closed floor (item 06: `log_closed_count`);\\n          per graph Harper's bound (`harper_bound_graph`, `--max-t` levels,\\n          `--budget` seconds, censoring recorded).\\n  stats   per `n`, the quantiles of every consecutive difference of the ladder,\\n          the violation counts (a floor above `pw` at `< 0.01` is the stop\\n          condition of TASK.md), and where the slack sits.\\n  draw    the ladder figure (medians per `n`, gap to `pw`), PNG.\\n\\nOutputs here: ledger_6_1.csv, ledger_gnp.csv, cells_gnp.csv, summary.csv,\\nladder.png, run.log.\\n\\nRegenerate: nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger/run.py --workers 6\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport argparse\\nimport csv\\nimport math\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nimport time\\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \\\"..\\\", \\\"..\\\", \\\"..\\\", \\\"..\\\"))\\nHERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\\nsys.path.insert(0, ROOT)\\nos.chdir(ROOT)\\n\\nfrom learning import separator_moment as sm  # noqa: E402\\nfrom learning.first_moment import floors as pair_floors, log_bound, lchoose  # noqa: E402\\n\\nLN10 = math.log(10)\\nSLACK = \\\"reports/scratch/structured_count/slack_6_1.csv\\\"\\nPILOT = \\\"reports/scratch/gnp_pilot/results.csv\\\"\\nTHRESH = {\\\"lt1\\\": 1.0, \\\"lt001\\\": 0.01}\\n\\n\\ndef log(msg: str = \\\"\\\") -> None:\\n    print(msg, flush=True)\\n    with open(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"run.log\\\"), \\\"a\\\") as f:\\n        f.write(msg + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef write_csv(path: str, rows: list[dict]) -> None:\\n    with open(path, \\\"w\\\", newline=\\\"\\\") as f:\\n        w = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=list(rows[0].keys()))\\n        w.writeheader()\\n        w.writerows(rows)\\n\\n\\ndef read_csv(path: str) -> list[dict]:\\n    with open(path) as f:\\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\\n\\n\\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ covers\\n\\ndef cover_task(args):\\n    frame, cell_text, index, name, rec = args\\n    from learning.ensemble import Cell, generate\\n    t0 = time.time()\\n    inst = generate(Cell(cell_text[0], cell_text[1], cell_text[2], cell_text[3]), index)\\n    assert inst.name == name, (inst.name, name)\\n    sizes = [int(s) for s in np.asarray(inst.matrix).sum(axis=0)]\\n    n = inst.n_customers\\n    assert n == int(rec[\\\"n\\\"]) and inst.n_patterns == int(rec[\\\"m\\\"])\\n    pw = int(rec[\\\"optimum\\\"]) - 1\\n    old = {k: log_bound(n, sizes, k) for k in range(n)}\\n    xp = {k: sm.cover_log_pair_bound(n, k, sizes) for k in range(n)}\\n    o1, o2 = sm.floor_pw(old, 1.0), sm.floor_pw(old, 0.01)\\n    x1, x2 = sm.floor_pw(xp, 1.0), sm.floor_pw(xp, 0.01)\\n    # the record's floors (optimum scale) must be these plus one\\n    f_old = pair_floors(n, sizes)\\n    assert (o1 + 1, o2 + 1) == f_old == (int(rec[\\\"floor_old\\\"]), int(rec[\\\"floor_old_001\\\"])), (name, o1, o2, f_old, rec)\\n    assert (x1 + 1, x2 + 1) == (int(rec[\\\"floor_1\\\"]), int(rec[\\\"floor_1_001\\\"])), (name, x1, x2, rec)\\n    # closed and flip around the exact-size floors (each k is its own statement; the window holds the floors)\\n    ks = list(range(max(0, x2 - 5), min(n - 1, max(x1 + 7, pw + 1)) + 1))\\n    cl = {k: sm.closed_cover_log_bound(n, k, sizes, optimise=False) for k in ks}\\n    fl = {k: sm.flip_log_bound_fast(n, k, sizes)[0] for k in ks}\\n    c1, c2 = sm.floor_pw(cl, 1.0), sm.floor_pw(cl, 0.01)\\n    f1, f2 = sm.floor_pw(fl, 1.0), sm.floor_pw(fl, 0.01)\\n    harper = int(rec[\\\"harper\\\"]) - 1          # the record's value is on the MOSP scale\\n    return {\\\"frame\\\": frame, \\\"instance\\\": name, \\\"n\\\": n, \\\"m\\\": inst.n_patterns, \\\"pw\\\": pw,\\n            \\\"old_lt1\\\": o1, \\\"xpair_lt1\\\": x1, \\\"closed_lt1\\\": c1, \\\"flip_lt1\\\": f1,\\n            \\\"old_lt001\\\": o2, \\\"xpair_lt001\\\": x2, \\\"closed_lt001\\\": c2, \\\"flip_lt001\\\": f2,\\n            \\\"best_lt1\\\": max(c1, f1, x1), \\\"best_lt001\\\": max(c2, f2, x2),\\n            \\\"harper\\\": harper, \\\"harper_cap\\\": int(rec[\\\"cap\\\"]), \\\"harper_complete\\\": rec[\\\"complete\\\"] == \\\"True\\\",\\n            \\\"harper_secs\\\": round(float(rec[\\\"secs\\\"]), 1),\\n            \\\"log10_old_at_pw\\\": old[pw] / LN10, \\\"log10_xpair_at_pw\\\": xp[pw] / LN10,\\n            \\\"log10_closed_at_pw\\\": cl.get(pw, float(\\\"nan\\\")) / LN10, \\\"log10_flip_at_pw\\\": fl.get(pw, float(\\\"nan\\\")) / LN10,\\n            \\\"k_scanned\\\": f\\\"{ks[0]}-{ks[-1]}\\\", \\\"seconds\\\": round(time.time() - t0, 2)}\\n\\n\\ndef stage_covers(workers: int) -> None:\\n    import pandas as pd\\n    log(\\\"== covers: the 600 certified (6, 1) instances with Harper on record ==\\\")\\n    t0 = time.time()\\n    rec = {r[\\\"instance\\\"]: r for r in read_csv(SLACK)}\\n    tasks = []\\n    for frame in (\\\"results.csv\\\", \\\"results_upward.csv\\\"):\\n        df = pd.read_csv(f\\\"learning/data/ensemble/{frame}\\\")\\n        sub = df[(df.generator == \\\"fixed\\\") & (df.param == 6) & (df.m == df.n) & (df.n >= 30)]\\n        assert sub.certified.all()\\n        for r in sub.itertuples():\\n            assert r.instance_name in rec and int(rec[r.instance_name][\\\"optimum\\\"]) == int(r.optimum)\\n            tasks.append((frame, (r.generator, int(r.n), int(r.m), float(r.param)), int(r.index), r.instance_name, rec[r.instance_name]))\\n    assert len(tasks) == len(rec) == 600, (len(tasks), len(rec))\\n    tasks.sort(key=lambda t: -t[1][1])\\n    with Pool(workers) as pool:\\n        rows = pool.map(cover_task, tasks, chunksize=2)\\n    rows.sort(key=lambda r: (r[\\\"n\\\"], r[\\\"instance\\\"]))\\n    write_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"ledger_6_1.csv\\\"), rows)\\n    log(f\\\"covers: {len(rows)} instances in {time.time() - t0:.0f} s wall ({sum(r['seconds'] for r in rows) / 3600:.2f} core-hours of bounds; Harper read from the record)\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ gnp\\n\\ndef cell_task(args):\\n    n, c = args\\n    p = c / n\\n    t0 = time.time()\\n    lc = sm.log_connected(n, p)\\n    rows = []\\n    for k in range(n):\\n        N, t = sm.forced_sizes(n, k)\\n        lck = lchoose(n, k)\\n        rows.append({\\\"n\\\": n, \\\"c\\\": c, \\\"k\\\": k, \\\"N\\\": N, \\\"t\\\": t,\\n                     \\\"logB_old\\\": lchoose(n, t) + lchoose(n - t, t - 1) + t * (t - 1) * math.log1p(-p) if t >= 1 else math.inf,\\n                     \\\"logB_xpair\\\": lck + sm.log_product_bound(N, p, t),\\n                     \\\"logB_sep\\\": lck + sm.log_prob_bip(N, p, t, lc),\\n                     \\\"logB_closed\\\": sm.log_closed_count(n, k, p)})\\n    return n, c, rows, time.time() - t0\\n\\n\\ndef harper_task(args):\\n    n, c, sample, seed, width, m, max_t, budget = args\\n    adj = sm.gnp_masks(n, c / n, seed)\\n    assert sum(popc(a) for a in adj) // 2 == m, (n, c, seed)\\n    hb = sm.harper_bound_graph(adj, max_t=max_t, time_budget=budget)\\n    return {\\\"n\\\": n, \\\"c\\\": c, \\\"sample\\\": sample, \\\"seed\\\": seed, \\\"pw\\\": width, \\\"harper\\\": hb.value, \\\"harper_cap\\\": hb.cap,\\n            \\\"harper_levels\\\": \\\" \\\".join(map(str, hb.levels)), \\\"harper_complete\\\": hb.complete, \\\"harper_secs\\\": round(hb.seconds, 1)}\\n\\n\\ndef popc(x: int) -> int:\\n    return bin(x).count(\\\"1\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef stage_gnp(workers: int, max_t: int, budget: float) -> None:\\n    log(f\\\"== gnp: the pilot's c = 10 cells at n = 30–60, proved graphs; Harper with max_t {max_t}, budget {budget:.0f} s ==\\\")\\n    t0 = time.time()\\n    pilot = [r for r in read_csv(PILOT) if float(r[\\\"c\\\"]) == 10 and int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) in (30, 40, 50, 60)]\\n    proved = [r for r in pilot if r[\\\"status\\\"] != \\\"upper\\\"]\\n    for r in proved:\\n        assert int(r[\\\"lower\\\"]) == int(r[\\\"width\\\"]), r\\n    log(f\\\"  {len(pilot)} graphs in the four cells, {len(proved)} proved ({sum(1 for r in pilot if r['status'] == 'minor')} by a minor certificate)\\\")\\n    # the layout on record has the width (both orientations tried: the C program's convention is not pinned here)\\n    bad = 0\\n    for r in proved:\\n        n = int(r[\\\"n\\\"])\\n        adj = sm.gnp_masks(n, 10 / n, int(r[\\\"seed\\\"]))\\n        lay = [int(x) for x in r[\\\"layout\\\"].split()]\\n        vs = min(sm.layout_vertex_separation(adj, lay), sm.layout_vertex_separation(adj, lay[::-1]))\\n        if vs != int(r[\\\"width\\\"]):\\n            bad += 1\\n    log(f\\\"  layout check: {len(proved) - bad} of {len(proved)} layouts have the recorded width in one orientation, {bad} do not\\\")\\n    with Pool(workers) as pool:\\n        cells = pool.map(cell_task, [(n, 10) for n in (30, 40, 50, 60)])\\n    cell_rows = []\\n    for n, c, rows, secs in cells:\\n        cell_rows.extend(rows)\\n    write_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"cells_gnp.csv\\\"), cell_rows)\\n    log(f\\\"  cell bounds: {len(cell_rows)} (n, k) rows in {sum(s for *_, s in cells):.0f} s\\\")\\n    tasks = [(int(r[\\\"n\\\"]), 10, int(r[\\\"sample\\\"]), int(r[\\\"seed\\\"]), int(r[\\\"width\\\"]), int(r[\\\"m\\\"]), max_t, budget) for r in proved]\\n    tasks.sort(key=lambda t: -t[0])\\n    with Pool(workers) as pool:\\n        rows = pool.map(harper_task, tasks, chunksize=1)\\n    by_cell = {}\\n    for r in cell_rows:\\n        by_cell.setdefault(int(r[\\\"n\\\"]), {})[int(r[\\\"k\\\"])] = r\\n    for r in rows:\\n        kb = by_cell[r[\\\"n\\\"]]\\n        for key, lab in ((\\\"logB_old\\\", \\\"old\\\"), (\\\"logB_xpair\\\", \\\"xpair\\\"), (\\\"logB_sep\\\", \\\"sep\\\"), (\\\"logB_closed\\\", \\\"closed\\\")):\\n            vals = {k: float(v[key]) for k, v in kb.items()}\\n            r[f\\\"{lab}_lt1\\\"] = sm.floor_pw(vals, 1.0)\\n            r[f\\\"{lab}_lt001\\\"] = sm.floor_pw(vals, 0.01)\\n            r[f\\\"log10_{lab}_at_pw\\\"] = vals[r[\\\"pw\\\"]] / LN10\\n        r[\\\"best_lt1\\\"] = max(r[\\\"sep_lt1\\\"], r[\\\"closed_lt1\\\"], r[\\\"xpair_lt1\\\"])\\n        r[\\\"best_lt001\\\"] = max(r[\\\"sep_lt001\\\"], r[\\\"closed_lt001\\\"], r[\\\"xpair_lt001\\\"])\\n    rows.sort(key=lambda r: (r[\\\"n\\\"], r[\\\"sample\\\"]))\\n    write_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"ledger_gnp.csv\\\"), rows)\\n    log(f\\\"gnp: {len(rows)} graphs in {time.time() - t0:.0f} s wall ({sum(r['harper_secs'] for r in rows) / 3600:.2f} core-hours of Harper)\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ stats\\n\\ndef q(vals, ps=(10, 50, 90)):\\n    return \\\" / \\\".join(f\\\"{np.percentile(vals, p):.0f}\\\" for p in ps)\\n\\n\\ndef ledger_stats(rows: list[dict], model: str, counts: list[tuple[str, str]], thr: str) -> list[dict]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Per `n`: quantiles and means of the consecutive differences at threshold `thr`.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    out = []\\n    ns = sorted({int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) for r in rows})\\n    log(f\\\"\\\\n{model}, floors at < {THRESH[thr]} (pw scale; quantiles 10 / 50 / 90, mean in brackets)\\\")\\n    header = \\\"  n   N | \\\" + \\\" | \\\".join(f\\\"{b}−{a}\\\" for a, b in counts) + \\\" | Harper−best | pw−Harper | pw−best | share union-bound | Harper≥best | Harper=pw | viol\\\"\\n    log(header)\\n    for n in ns:\\n        g = [r for r in rows if int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) == n]\\n        pw = np.array([int(r[\\\"pw\\\"]) for r in g])\\n        best = np.array([int(r[f\\\"best_{thr}\\\"]) for r in g])\\n        harper = np.array([int(r[\\\"harper\\\"]) for r in g])\\n        d = {\\\"model\\\": model, \\\"thresh\\\": THRESH[thr], \\\"n\\\": n, \\\"N\\\": len(g), \\\"mean_pw\\\": pw.mean(), \\\"mean_harper\\\": harper.mean()}\\n        cells = []\\n        for a, b in counts:\\n            diff = np.array([int(r[f\\\"{b}_{thr}\\\"]) - int(r[f\\\"{a}_{thr}\\\"]) for r in g])\\n            d[f\\\"{b}_minus_{a}_mean\\\"] = diff.mean()\\n            d[f\\\"{b}_minus_{a}_q\\\"] = q(diff)\\n            d[f\\\"mean_{a}\\\"] = np.mean([int(r[f\\\"{a}_{thr}\\\"]) for r in g])\\n            d[f\\\"mean_{b}\\\"] = np.mean([int(r[f\\\"{b}_{thr}\\\"]) for r in g])\\n            cells.append(f\\\"{q(diff)} ({diff.mean():.2f})\\\")\\n        hb, ph, pb = harper - best, pw - harper, pw - best\\n        share = hb.sum() / pb.sum() if pb.sum() else float(\\\"nan\\\")\\n        d.update(harper_minus_best_mean=hb.mean(), harper_minus_best_q=q(hb), pw_minus_harper_mean=ph.mean(), pw_minus_harper_q=q(ph),\\n                 pw_minus_best_mean=pb.mean(), pw_minus_best_q=q(pb), share_union_bound=share,\\n                 harper_ge_best=int((hb >= 0).sum()), harper_eq_pw=int((ph == 0).sum()),\\n                 violations=int((best > pw).sum()), mean_best=best.mean(),\\n                 cap_min=min(int(r[\\\"harper_cap\\\"]) for r in g), cap_median=float(np.median([int(r[\\\"harper_cap\\\"]) for r in g])),\\n                 complete=sum(1 for r in g if str(r[\\\"harper_complete\\\"]) == \\\"True\\\"),\\n                 harper_secs_mean=float(np.mean([float(r[\\\"harper_secs\\\"]) for r in g])))\\n        log(f\\\"{n:4d} {len(g):3d} | \\\" + \\\" | \\\".join(cells) + f\\\" | {q(hb)} ({hb.mean():.2f}) | {q(ph)} ({ph.mean():.2f}) | {q(pb)} ({pb.mean():.2f}) | {share:.2f} | {d['harper_ge_best']} | {d['harper_eq_pw']} | {d['violations']}\\\")\\n        out.append(d)\\n    return out\\n\\n\\ndef stage_stats() -> None:\\n    log(\\\"\\\\n== stats ==\\\")\\n    cov = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"ledger_6_1.csv\\\"))\\n    gnp = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"ledger_gnp.csv\\\"))\\n    summary = []\\n    for thr in (\\\"lt001\\\", \\\"lt1\\\"):\\n        summary += ledger_stats(cov, \\\"covers (6, 1), fixed generator, m = n\\\", [(\\\"old\\\", \\\"xpair\\\"), (\\\"xpair\\\", \\\"closed\\\"), (\\\"xpair\\\", \\\"flip\\\")], thr)\\n        summary += ledger_stats(gnp, \\\"G(n, 10/n), pilot, proved\\\", [(\\\"old\\\", \\\"xpair\\\"), (\\\"xpair\\\", \\\"sep\\\"), (\\\"xpair\\\", \\\"closed\\\")], thr)\\n    write_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"summary.csv\\\"), summary)\\n    # violations at both thresholds, every count\\n    log(\\\"\\\\nviolations (floor > pw), by count and threshold:\\\")\\n    for name, rows, keys in ((\\\"covers\\\", cov, (\\\"old\\\", \\\"xpair\\\", \\\"closed\\\", \\\"flip\\\")), (\\\"gnp\\\", gnp, (\\\"old\\\", \\\"xpair\\\", \\\"sep\\\", \\\"closed\\\"))):\\n        for thr in (\\\"lt1\\\", \\\"lt001\\\"):\\n            v = {k: sum(1 for r in rows if int(r[f\\\"{k}_{thr}\\\"]) > int(r[\\\"pw\\\"])) for k in keys}\\n            log(f\\\"  {name} < {THRESH[thr]}: {v}\\\")\\n    # Harper censoring\\n    log(\\\"\\\\nHarper under the cap: covers (record, max_t 12, 60 s) and gnp (this item)\\\")\\n    for name, rows in ((\\\"covers\\\", cov), (\\\"gnp\\\", gnp)):\\n        for n in sorted({int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) for r in rows}):\\n            g = [r for r in rows if int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) == n]\\n            caps = [int(r[\\\"harper_cap\\\"]) for r in g]\\n            t_forced = [math.ceil((int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) - int(r[\\\"pw\\\"])) / 2) for r in g]\\n            log(f\\\"  {name} n={n}: cap min/median/max {min(caps)}/{np.median(caps):.0f}/{max(caps)}; forced t at pw: {min(t_forced)}–{max(t_forced)}; complete {sum(1 for r in g if str(r['harper_complete']) == 'True')}/{len(g)}; secs mean/max {np.mean([float(r['harper_secs']) for r in g]):.1f}/{max(float(r['harper_secs']) for r in g):.0f}\\\")\\n    # per-cell floors on gnp (same for every graph in a cell) and the decades at pw\\n    log(\\\"\\\\ngnp cells: floors (pw scale) at < 1 / < 0.01 and min/mean/max pw; log10 of each bound at k = min pw\\\")\\n    cells = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"cells_gnp.csv\\\"))\\n    for n in (30, 40, 50, 60):\\n        kb = {int(r[\\\"k\\\"]): r for r in cells if int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) == n}\\n        g = [int(r[\\\"pw\\\"]) for r in gnp if int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) == n]\\n        parts = []\\n        for key, lab in ((\\\"logB_old\\\", \\\"old\\\"), (\\\"logB_xpair\\\", \\\"xpair\\\"), (\\\"logB_sep\\\", \\\"sep\\\"), (\\\"logB_closed\\\", \\\"closed\\\")):\\n            vals = {k: float(v[key]) for k, v in kb.items()}\\n            parts.append(f\\\"{lab} {sm.floor_pw(vals, 1.0)}/{sm.floor_pw(vals, 0.01)} ({vals[min(g)] / LN10:+.2f})\\\")\\n        log(f\\\"  n={n}: \\\" + \\\"; \\\".join(parts) + f\\\"; pw {min(g)}/{np.mean(g):.1f}/{max(g)}\\\")\\n    # the decades at k = pw on covers (mean per n)\\n    log(\\\"\\\\ncovers: mean log10 of each count's bound at k = pw (the instance's own pathwidth)\\\")\\n    for n in sorted({int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) for r in cov}):\\n        g = [r for r in cov if int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) == n]\\n        log(f\\\"  n={n}: old {np.mean([float(r['log10_old_at_pw']) for r in g]):+.2f}, xpair {np.mean([float(r['log10_xpair_at_pw']) for r in g]):+.2f}, \\\"\\n            f\\\"closed {np.nanmean([float(r['log10_closed_at_pw']) for r in g]):+.2f}, flip {np.nanmean([float(r['log10_flip_at_pw']) for r in g]):+.2f}\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ draw\\n\\ndef stage_draw() -> None:\\n    import matplotlib\\n    matplotlib.use(\\\"Agg\\\")\\n    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n    cov = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"ledger_6_1.csv\\\"))\\n    gnp = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"ledger_gnp.csv\\\"))\\n    # palette: reference categorical slots 1, 2, 3, 4 and text-primary for pw (validated, see run.log)\\n    rungs_cov = [(\\\"old_lt001\\\", \\\"old pair floor\\\", \\\"#2a78d6\\\"), (\\\"xpair_lt001\\\", \\\"exact-size pair floor\\\", \\\"#eb6834\\\"),\\n                 (\\\"best_lt001\\\", \\\"best count (closed / flip)\\\", \\\"#1baf7a\\\"), (\\\"harper\\\", \\\"Harper (capped)\\\", \\\"#eda100\\\"), (\\\"pw\\\", \\\"pathwidth\\\", \\\"#0b0b0b\\\")]\\n    rungs_gnp = [(\\\"old_lt001\\\", \\\"old pair floor\\\", \\\"#2a78d6\\\"), (\\\"xpair_lt001\\\", \\\"exact-size pair floor\\\", \\\"#eb6834\\\"),\\n                 (\\\"best_lt001\\\", \\\"best count (separator / closed)\\\", \\\"#1baf7a\\\"), (\\\"harper\\\", \\\"Harper (capped)\\\", \\\"#eda100\\\"), (\\\"pw\\\", \\\"pathwidth\\\", \\\"#0b0b0b\\\")]\\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(10.5, 4.4), sharey=True)\\n    for ax, rows, rungs, title in ((axes[0], cov, rungs_cov, \\\"random clique covers (6, 1), m = n, certified\\\"),\\n                                   (axes[1], gnp, rungs_gnp, \\\"G(n, 10/n), pilot graphs, proved\\\")):\\n        ns = sorted({int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) for r in rows})\\n        for i, n in enumerate(ns):\\n            g = [r for r in rows if int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) == n]\\n            pw = np.array([int(r[\\\"pw\\\"]) for r in g])\\n            meds = []\\n            for key, lab, col in rungs:\\n                gap = pw - np.array([int(r[key]) for r in g])\\n                meds.append(float(np.median(gap)))\\n            ax.plot([n, n], [max(meds), min(meds)], color=\\\"#c3c2b7\\\", linewidth=1.5, zorder=1)\\n            for (key, lab, col), m in zip(rungs, meds):\\n                ax.plot([n], [m], \\\"o\\\", color=col, markersize=8, markeredgecolor=\\\"#fcfcfb\\\", markeredgewidth=1.2, zorder=3,\\n                        label=lab if i == 0 else None)\\n                if i == len(ns) - 1:\\n                    ax.annotate(lab, (n, m), xytext=(8, 0), textcoords=\\\"offset points\\\", fontsize=8, color=\\\"#52514e\\\", va=\\\"center\\\")\\n        ax.set_xlabel(\\\"n\\\")\\n        ax.set_title(title, fontsize=9, color=\\\"#52514e\\\", loc=\\\"left\\\")\\n        ax.set_xticks(ns)\\n        ax.set_xlim(min(ns) - 3, max(ns) + 22)\\n        ax.grid(axis=\\\"y\\\", color=\\\"#e8e7e3\\\", linewidth=0.8)\\n        for s in (\\\"top\\\", \\\"right\\\"):\\n            ax.spines[s].set_visible(False)\\n        ax.spines[\\\"left\\\"].set_color(\\\"#c3c2b7\\\")\\n        ax.spines[\\\"bottom\\\"].set_color(\\\"#c3c2b7\\\")\\n    axes[0].set_ylabel(\\\"stacks below the pathwidth (median per n)\\\")\\n    axes[0].invert_yaxis()\\n    axes[0].legend(loc=\\\"lower left\\\", fontsize=8, frameon=False)\\n    fig.tight_layout()\\n    fig.savefig(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"ladder.png\\\"), dpi=160)\\n    log(\\\"draw: ladder.png\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef main() -> None:\\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--stage\\\", default=\\\"all\\\", choices=[\\\"all\\\", \\\"covers\\\", \\\"gnp\\\", \\\"stats\\\", \\\"draw\\\"])\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--workers\\\", type=int, default=6)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--max-t\\\", type=int, default=16)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--budget\\\", type=float, default=60.0)\\n    a = ap.parse_args()\\n    if a.stage in (\\\"all\\\", \\\"covers\\\"):\\n        stage_covers(a.workers)\\n    if a.stage in (\\\"all\\\", \\\"gnp\\\"):\\n        stage_gnp(a.workers, a.max_t, a.budget)\\n    if a.stage in (\\\"all\\\", \\\"stats\\\"):\\n        stage_stats()\\n    if a.stage in (\\\"all\\\", \\\"draw\\\"):\\n        stage_draw()\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\nEOF\\nuptime; rm -f reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger/run.log; nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger/run.py --stage covers --workers 6 2>&1 | tail -5\",\"description\":\"Write the ledger script and run the covers stage\",\"timeout\":600000},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":32,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1155,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":175245,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1155,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":4,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"c821cc2c-f627-4785-bc52-942e492e87f6\",\"uuid\":\"af88cafa-97ab-43fc-b04e-0f1e06c04410\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-01T21:44:48.773Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgcwLHn6aJM5Gd5VbCBX3\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01AfUfM8SNXHdwJV5R5JBATC\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/al/dev/MOSP && mkdir -p reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger && cat > reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger/run.py <<'EOF'\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"loop0011 item 11: the slack ledger — in stacks, what each count buys and what\\nis left, on certified instances (`reports/separator_moment.md` §11).\\n\\nEvery quantity is on the *pathwidth* scale (`pw = optimum − 1` on covers; the\\nproved width on the pilot graphs).  A floor at threshold `θ` is the largest `k`\\nwith the count's bound on `P(pw ≤ k)` below `θ`, plus one (`learning.\\nseparator_moment.floor_pw`; the record's `floors` is this plus one more, for\\nthe optimum).  The ladder per instance is\\n\\n    old pair → exact-size pair → {closed, flip | separator, closed} → Harper → pw,\\n\\nwhere `Harper` is the vertex-isoperimetric bound under a level cap and a time\\nbudget (a *lower* bound on the true Harper value, which is itself ≤ pw), so\\n`pw − Harper` is an *upper* bound on the necessary condition's slack and\\n`Harper − floor` a *lower* bound on the union bound's (§8.5 (b) of\\n`reports/excess_phase_diagram.md`).\\n\\nStages (`--stage covers|gnp|stats|draw`, all by default):\\n  covers  the 600 certified `(6, 1)` fixed-generator instances at `n = m = 30–75`\\n          whose Harper values are on record (`reports/scratch/structured_count/\\n          slack_6_1.csv`, read, never re-solved): sizes regenerated from the\\n          seeds (`learning.ensemble.generate`), the old pair floor, the\\n          exact-size pair floor, the closed-pair floor (NA bound, item 07) and the\\n          flip floor (item 07), at `< 1` and `< 0.01`.\\n  gnp     the pilot's `c = 10` cells at `n = 30, 40, 50, 60` (`reports/scratch/\\n          gnp_pilot/results.csv`, proved graphs only, regenerated from their\\n          seeds; the layout re-checked against the width): per cell the old and\\n          exact-size pair floors, the separator floor (item 05: `C(n, k)\\n          P_N(E_bip)`, exact) and the closed floor (item 06: `log_closed_count`);\\n          per graph Harper's bound (`harper_bound_graph`, `--max-t` levels,\\n          `--budget` seconds, censoring recorded).\\n  stats   per `n`, the quantiles of every consecutive difference of the ladder,\\n          the violation counts (a floor above `pw` at `< 0.01` is the stop\\n          condition of TASK.md), and where the slack sits.\\n  draw    the ladder figure (medians per `n`, gap to `pw`), PNG.\\n\\nOutputs here: ledger_6_1.csv, ledger_gnp.csv, cells_gnp.csv, summary.csv,\\nladder.png, run.log.\\n\\nRegenerate: nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger/run.py --workers 6\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport argparse\\nimport csv\\nimport math\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nimport time\\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \\\"..\\\", \\\"..\\\", \\\"..\\\", \\\"..\\\"))\\nHERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\\nsys.path.insert(0, ROOT)\\nos.chdir(ROOT)\\n\\nfrom learning import separator_moment as sm  # noqa: E402\\nfrom learning.first_moment import floors as pair_floors, log_bound, lchoose  # noqa: E402\\n\\nLN10 = math.log(10)\\nSLACK = \\\"reports/scratch/structured_count/slack_6_1.csv\\\"\\nPILOT = \\\"reports/scratch/gnp_pilot/results.csv\\\"\\nTHRESH = {\\\"lt1\\\": 1.0, \\\"lt001\\\": 0.01}\\n\\n\\ndef log(msg: str = \\\"\\\") -> None:\\n    print(msg, flush=True)\\n    with open(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"run.log\\\"), \\\"a\\\") as f:\\n        f.write(msg + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef write_csv(path: str, rows: list[dict]) -> None:\\n    with open(path, \\\"w\\\", newline=\\\"\\\") as f:\\n        w = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=list(rows[0].keys()))\\n        w.writeheader()\\n        w.writerows(rows)\\n\\n\\ndef read_csv(path: str) -> list[dict]:\\n    with open(path) as f:\\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\\n\\n\\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ covers\\n\\ndef cover_task(args):\\n    frame, cell_text, index, name, rec = args\\n    from learning.ensemble import Cell, generate\\n    t0 = time.time()\\n    inst = generate(Cell(cell_text[0], cell_text[1], cell_text[2], cell_text[3]), index)\\n    assert inst.name == name, (inst.name, name)\\n    sizes = [int(s) for s in np.asarray(inst.matrix).sum(axis=0)]\\n    n = inst.n_customers\\n    assert n == int(rec[\\\"n\\\"]) and inst.n_patterns == int(rec[\\\"m\\\"])\\n    pw = int(rec[\\\"optimum\\\"]) - 1\\n    old = {k: log_bound(n, sizes, k) for k in range(n)}\\n    xp = {k: sm.cover_log_pair_bound(n, k, sizes) for k in range(n)}\\n    o1, o2 = sm.floor_pw(old, 1.0), sm.floor_pw(old, 0.01)\\n    x1, x2 = sm.floor_pw(xp, 1.0), sm.floor_pw(xp, 0.01)\\n    # the record's floors (optimum scale) must be these plus one\\n    f_old = pair_floors(n, sizes)\\n    assert (o1 + 1, o2 + 1) == f_old == (int(rec[\\\"floor_old\\\"]), int(rec[\\\"floor_old_001\\\"])), (name, o1, o2, f_old, rec)\\n    assert (x1 + 1, x2 + 1) == (int(rec[\\\"floor_1\\\"]), int(rec[\\\"floor_1_001\\\"])), (name, x1, x2, rec)\\n    # closed and flip around the exact-size floors (each k is its own statement; the window holds the floors)\\n    ks = list(range(max(0, x2 - 5), min(n - 1, max(x1 + 7, pw + 1)) + 1))\\n    cl = {k: sm.closed_cover_log_bound(n, k, sizes, optimise=False) for k in ks}\\n    fl = {k: sm.flip_log_bound_fast(n, k, sizes)[0] for k in ks}\\n    c1, c2 = sm.floor_pw(cl, 1.0), sm.floor_pw(cl, 0.01)\\n    f1, f2 = sm.floor_pw(fl, 1.0), sm.floor_pw(fl, 0.01)\\n    harper = int(rec[\\\"harper\\\"]) - 1          # the record's value is on the MOSP scale\\n    return {\\\"frame\\\": frame, \\\"instance\\\": name, \\\"n\\\": n, \\\"m\\\": inst.n_patterns, \\\"pw\\\": pw,\\n            \\\"old_lt1\\\": o1, \\\"xpair_lt1\\\": x1, \\\"closed_lt1\\\": c1, \\\"flip_lt1\\\": f1,\\n            \\\"old_lt001\\\": o2, \\\"xpair_lt001\\\": x2, \\\"closed_lt001\\\": c2, \\\"flip_lt001\\\": f2,\\n            \\\"best_lt1\\\": max(c1, f1, x1), \\\"best_lt001\\\": max(c2, f2, x2),\\n            \\\"harper\\\": harper, \\\"harper_cap\\\": int(rec[\\\"cap\\\"]), \\\"harper_complete\\\": rec[\\\"complete\\\"] == \\\"True\\\",\\n            \\\"harper_secs\\\": round(float(rec[\\\"secs\\\"]), 1),\\n            \\\"log10_old_at_pw\\\": old[pw] / LN10, \\\"log10_xpair_at_pw\\\": xp[pw] / LN10,\\n            \\\"log10_closed_at_pw\\\": cl.get(pw, float(\\\"nan\\\")) / LN10, \\\"log10_flip_at_pw\\\": fl.get(pw, float(\\\"nan\\\")) / LN10,\\n            \\\"k_scanned\\\": f\\\"{ks[0]}-{ks[-1]}\\\", \\\"seconds\\\": round(time.time() - t0, 2)}\\n\\n\\ndef stage_covers(workers: int) -> None:\\n    import pandas as pd\\n    log(\\\"== covers: the 600 certified (6, 1) instances with Harper on record ==\\\")\\n    t0 = time.time()\\n    rec = {r[\\\"instance\\\"]: r for r in read_csv(SLACK)}\\n    tasks = []\\n    for frame in (\\\"results.csv\\\", \\\"results_upward.csv\\\"):\\n        df = pd.read_csv(f\\\"learning/data/ensemble/{frame}\\\")\\n        sub = df[(df.generator == \\\"fixed\\\") & (df.param == 6) & (df.m == df.n) & (df.n >= 30)]\\n        assert sub.certified.all()\\n        for r in sub.itertuples():\\n            assert r.instance_name in rec and int(rec[r.instance_name][\\\"optimum\\\"]) == int(r.optimum)\\n            tasks.append((frame, (r.generator, int(r.n), int(r.m), float(r.param)), int(r.index), r.instance_name, rec[r.instance_name]))\\n    assert len(tasks) == len(rec) == 600, (len(tasks), len(rec))\\n    tasks.sort(key=lambda t: -t[1][1])\\n    with Pool(workers) as pool:\\n        rows = pool.map(cover_task, tasks, chunksize=2)\\n    rows.sort(key=lambda r: (r[\\\"n\\\"], r[\\\"instance\\\"]))\\n    write_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"ledger_6_1.csv\\\"), rows)\\n    log(f\\\"covers: {len(rows)} instances in {time.time() - t0:.0f} s wall ({sum(r['seconds'] for r in rows) / 3600:.2f} core-hours of bounds; Harper read from the record)\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ gnp\\n\\ndef cell_task(args):\\n    n, c = args\\n    p = c / n\\n    t0 = time.time()\\n    lc = sm.log_connected(n, p)\\n    rows = []\\n    for k in range(n):\\n        N, t = sm.forced_sizes(n, k)\\n        lck = lchoose(n, k)\\n        rows.append({\\\"n\\\": n, \\\"c\\\": c, \\\"k\\\": k, \\\"N\\\": N, \\\"t\\\": t,\\n                     \\\"logB_old\\\": lchoose(n, t) + lchoose(n - t, t - 1) + t * (t - 1) * math.log1p(-p) if t >= 1 else math.inf,\\n                     \\\"logB_xpair\\\": lck + sm.log_product_bound(N, p, t),\\n                     \\\"logB_sep\\\": lck + sm.log_prob_bip(N, p, t, lc),\\n                     \\\"logB_closed\\\": sm.log_closed_count(n, k, p)})\\n    return n, c, rows, time.time() - t0\\n\\n\\ndef harper_task(args):\\n    n, c, sample, seed, width, m, max_t, budget = args\\n    adj = sm.gnp_masks(n, c / n, seed)\\n    assert sum(popc(a) for a in adj) // 2 == m, (n, c, seed)\\n    hb = sm.harper_bound_graph(adj, max_t=max_t, time_budget=budget)\\n    return {\\\"n\\\": n, \\\"c\\\": c, \\\"sample\\\": sample, \\\"seed\\\": seed, \\\"pw\\\": width, \\\"harper\\\": hb.value, \\\"harper_cap\\\": hb.cap,\\n            \\\"harper_levels\\\": \\\" \\\".join(map(str, hb.levels)), \\\"harper_complete\\\": hb.complete, \\\"harper_secs\\\": round(hb.seconds, 1)}\\n\\n\\ndef popc(x: int) -> int:\\n    return bin(x).count(\\\"1\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef stage_gnp(workers: int, max_t: int, budget: float) -> None:\\n    log(f\\\"== gnp: the pilot's c = 10 cells at n = 30–60, proved graphs; Harper with max_t {max_t}, budget {budget:.0f} s ==\\\")\\n    t0 = time.time()\\n    pilot = [r for r in read_csv(PILOT) if float(r[\\\"c\\\"]) == 10 and int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) in (30, 40, 50, 60)]\\n    proved = [r for r in pilot if r[\\\"status\\\"] != \\\"upper\\\"]\\n    for r in proved:\\n        assert int(r[\\\"lower\\\"]) == int(r[\\\"width\\\"]), r\\n    log(f\\\"  {len(pilot)} graphs in the four cells, {len(proved)} proved ({sum(1 for r in pilot if r['status'] == 'minor')} by a minor certificate)\\\")\\n    # the layout on record has the width (both orientations tried: the C program's convention is not pinned here)\\n    bad = 0\\n    for r in proved:\\n        n = int(r[\\\"n\\\"])\\n        adj = sm.gnp_masks(n, 10 / n, int(r[\\\"seed\\\"]))\\n        lay = [int(x) for x in r[\\\"layout\\\"].split()]\\n        vs = min(sm.layout_vertex_separation(adj, lay), sm.layout_vertex_separation(adj, lay[::-1]))\\n        if vs != int(r[\\\"width\\\"]):\\n            bad += 1\\n    log(f\\\"  layout check: {len(proved) - bad} of {len(proved)} layouts have the recorded width in one orientation, {bad} do not\\\")\\n    with Pool(workers) as pool:\\n        cells = pool.map(cell_task, [(n, 10) for n in (30, 40, 50, 60)])\\n    cell_rows = []\\n    for n, c, rows, secs in cells:\\n        cell_rows.extend(rows)\\n    write_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"cells_gnp.csv\\\"), cell_rows)\\n    log(f\\\"  cell bounds: {len(cell_rows)} (n, k) rows in {sum(s for *_, s in cells):.0f} s\\\")\\n    tasks = [(int(r[\\\"n\\\"]), 10, int(r[\\\"sample\\\"]), int(r[\\\"seed\\\"]), int(r[\\\"width\\\"]), int(r[\\\"m\\\"]), max_t, budget) for r in proved]\\n    tasks.sort(key=lambda t: -t[0])\\n    with Pool(workers) as pool:\\n        rows = pool.map(harper_task, tasks, chunksize=1)\\n    by_cell = {}\\n    for r in cell_rows:\\n        by_cell.setdefault(int(r[\\\"n\\\"]), {})[int(r[\\\"k\\\"])] = r\\n    for r in rows:\\n        kb = by_cell[r[\\\"n\\\"]]\\n        for key, lab in ((\\\"logB_old\\\", \\\"old\\\"), (\\\"logB_xpair\\\", \\\"xpair\\\"), (\\\"logB_sep\\\", \\\"sep\\\"), (\\\"logB_closed\\\", \\\"closed\\\")):\\n            vals = {k: float(v[key]) for k, v in kb.items()}\\n            r[f\\\"{lab}_lt1\\\"] = sm.floor_pw(vals, 1.0)\\n            r[f\\\"{lab}_lt001\\\"] = sm.floor_pw(vals, 0.01)\\n            r[f\\\"log10_{lab}_at_pw\\\"] = vals[r[\\\"pw\\\"]] / LN10\\n        r[\\\"best_lt1\\\"] = max(r[\\\"sep_lt1\\\"], r[\\\"closed_lt1\\\"], r[\\\"xpair_lt1\\\"])\\n        r[\\\"best_lt001\\\"] = max(r[\\\"sep_lt001\\\"], r[\\\"closed_lt001\\\"], r[\\\"xpair_lt001\\\"])\\n    rows.sort(key=lambda r: (r[\\\"n\\\"], r[\\\"sample\\\"]))\\n    write_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"ledger_gnp.csv\\\"), rows)\\n    log(f\\\"gnp: {len(rows)} graphs in {time.time() - t0:.0f} s wall ({sum(r['harper_secs'] for r in rows) / 3600:.2f} core-hours of Harper)\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ stats\\n\\ndef q(vals, ps=(10, 50, 90)):\\n    return \\\" / \\\".join(f\\\"{np.percentile(vals, p):.0f}\\\" for p in ps)\\n\\n\\ndef ledger_stats(rows: list[dict], model: str, counts: list[tuple[str, str]], thr: str) -> list[dict]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Per `n`: quantiles and means of the consecutive differences at threshold `thr`.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    out = []\\n    ns = sorted({int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) for r in rows})\\n    log(f\\\"\\\\n{model}, floors at < {THRESH[thr]} (pw scale; quantiles 10 / 50 / 90, mean in brackets)\\\")\\n    header = \\\"  n   N | \\\" + \\\" | \\\".join(f\\\"{b}−{a}\\\" for a, b in counts) + \\\" | Harper−best | pw−Harper | pw−best | share union-bound | Harper≥best | Harper=pw | viol\\\"\\n    log(header)\\n    for n in ns:\\n        g = [r for r in rows if int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) == n]\\n        pw = np.array([int(r[\\\"pw\\\"]) for r in g])\\n        best = np.array([int(r[f\\\"best_{thr}\\\"]) for r in g])\\n        harper = np.array([int(r[\\\"harper\\\"]) for r in g])\\n        d = {\\\"model\\\": model, \\\"thresh\\\": THRESH[thr], \\\"n\\\": n, \\\"N\\\": len(g), \\\"mean_pw\\\": pw.mean(), \\\"mean_harper\\\": harper.mean()}\\n        cells = []\\n        for a, b in counts:\\n            diff = np.array([int(r[f\\\"{b}_{thr}\\\"]) - int(r[f\\\"{a}_{thr}\\\"]) for r in g])\\n            d[f\\\"{b}_minus_{a}_mean\\\"] = diff.mean()\\n            d[f\\\"{b}_minus_{a}_q\\\"] = q(diff)\\n            d[f\\\"mean_{a}\\\"] = np.mean([int(r[f\\\"{a}_{thr}\\\"]) for r in g])\\n            d[f\\\"mean_{b}\\\"] = np.mean([int(r[f\\\"{b}_{thr}\\\"]) for r in g])\\n            cells.append(f\\\"{q(diff)} ({diff.mean():.2f})\\\")\\n        hb, ph, pb = harper - best, pw - harper, pw - best\\n        share = hb.sum() / pb.sum() if pb.sum() else float(\\\"nan\\\")\\n        d.update(harper_minus_best_mean=hb.mean(), harper_minus_best_q=q(hb), pw_minus_harper_mean=ph.mean(), pw_minus_harper_q=q(ph),\\n                 pw_minus_best_mean=pb.mean(), pw_minus_best_q=q(pb), share_union_bound=share,\\n                 harper_ge_best=int((hb >= 0).sum()), harper_eq_pw=int((ph == 0).sum()),\\n                 violations=int((best > pw).sum()), mean_best=best.mean(),\\n                 cap_min=min(int(r[\\\"harper_cap\\\"]) for r in g), cap_median=float(np.median([int(r[\\\"harper_cap\\\"]) for r in g])),\\n                 complete=sum(1 for r in g if str(r[\\\"harper_complete\\\"]) == \\\"True\\\"),\\n                 harper_secs_mean=float(np.mean([float(r[\\\"harper_secs\\\"]) for r in g])))\\n        log(f\\\"{n:4d} {len(g):3d} | \\\" + \\\" | \\\".join(cells) + f\\\" | {q(hb)} ({hb.mean():.2f}) | {q(ph)} ({ph.mean():.2f}) | {q(pb)} ({pb.mean():.2f}) | {share:.2f} | {d['harper_ge_best']} | {d['harper_eq_pw']} | {d['violations']}\\\")\\n        out.append(d)\\n    return out\\n\\n\\ndef stage_stats() -> None:\\n    log(\\\"\\\\n== stats ==\\\")\\n    cov = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"ledger_6_1.csv\\\"))\\n    gnp = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"ledger_gnp.csv\\\"))\\n    summary = []\\n    for thr in (\\\"lt001\\\", \\\"lt1\\\"):\\n        summary += ledger_stats(cov, \\\"covers (6, 1), fixed generator, m = n\\\", [(\\\"old\\\", \\\"xpair\\\"), (\\\"xpair\\\", \\\"closed\\\"), (\\\"xpair\\\", \\\"flip\\\")], thr)\\n        summary += ledger_stats(gnp, \\\"G(n, 10/n), pilot, proved\\\", [(\\\"old\\\", \\\"xpair\\\"), (\\\"xpair\\\", \\\"sep\\\"), (\\\"xpair\\\", \\\"closed\\\")], thr)\\n    write_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"summary.csv\\\"), summary)\\n    # violations at both thresholds, every count\\n    log(\\\"\\\\nviolations (floor > pw), by count and threshold:\\\")\\n    for name, rows, keys in ((\\\"covers\\\", cov, (\\\"old\\\", \\\"xpair\\\", \\\"closed\\\", \\\"flip\\\")), (\\\"gnp\\\", gnp, (\\\"old\\\", \\\"xpair\\\", \\\"sep\\\", \\\"closed\\\"))):\\n        for thr in (\\\"lt1\\\", \\\"lt001\\\"):\\n            v = {k: sum(1 for r in rows if int(r[f\\\"{k}_{thr}\\\"]) > int(r[\\\"pw\\\"])) for k in keys}\\n            log(f\\\"  {name} < {THRESH[thr]}: {v}\\\")\\n    # Harper censoring\\n    log(\\\"\\\\nHarper under the cap: covers (record, max_t 12, 60 s) and gnp (this item)\\\")\\n    for name, rows in ((\\\"covers\\\", cov), (\\\"gnp\\\", gnp)):\\n        for n in sorted({int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) for r in rows}):\\n            g = [r for r in rows if int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) == n]\\n            caps = [int(r[\\\"harper_cap\\\"]) for r in g]\\n            t_forced = [math.ceil((int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) - int(r[\\\"pw\\\"])) / 2) for r in g]\\n            log(f\\\"  {name} n={n}: cap min/median/max {min(caps)}/{np.median(caps):.0f}/{max(caps)}; forced t at pw: {min(t_forced)}–{max(t_forced)}; complete {sum(1 for r in g if str(r['harper_complete']) == 'True')}/{len(g)}; secs mean/max {np.mean([float(r['harper_secs']) for r in g]):.1f}/{max(float(r['harper_secs']) for r in g):.0f}\\\")\\n    # per-cell floors on gnp (same for every graph in a cell) and the decades at pw\\n    log(\\\"\\\\ngnp cells: floors (pw scale) at < 1 / < 0.01 and min/mean/max pw; log10 of each bound at k = min pw\\\")\\n    cells = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"cells_gnp.csv\\\"))\\n    for n in (30, 40, 50, 60):\\n        kb = {int(r[\\\"k\\\"]): r for r in cells if int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) == n}\\n        g = [int(r[\\\"pw\\\"]) for r in gnp if int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) == n]\\n        parts = []\\n        for key, lab in ((\\\"logB_old\\\", \\\"old\\\"), (\\\"logB_xpair\\\", \\\"xpair\\\"), (\\\"logB_sep\\\", \\\"sep\\\"), (\\\"logB_closed\\\", \\\"closed\\\")):\\n            vals = {k: float(v[key]) for k, v in kb.items()}\\n            parts.append(f\\\"{lab} {sm.floor_pw(vals, 1.0)}/{sm.floor_pw(vals, 0.01)} ({vals[min(g)] / LN10:+.2f})\\\")\\n        log(f\\\"  n={n}: \\\" + \\\"; \\\".join(parts) + f\\\"; pw {min(g)}/{np.mean(g):.1f}/{max(g)}\\\")\\n    # the decades at k = pw on covers (mean per n)\\n    log(\\\"\\\\ncovers: mean log10 of each count's bound at k = pw (the instance's own pathwidth)\\\")\\n    for n in sorted({int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) for r in cov}):\\n        g = [r for r in cov if int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) == n]\\n        log(f\\\"  n={n}: old {np.mean([float(r['log10_old_at_pw']) for r in g]):+.2f}, xpair {np.mean([float(r['log10_xpair_at_pw']) for r in g]):+.2f}, \\\"\\n            f\\\"closed {np.nanmean([float(r['log10_closed_at_pw']) for r in g]):+.2f}, flip {np.nanmean([float(r['log10_flip_at_pw']) for r in g]):+.2f}\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ draw\\n\\ndef stage_draw() -> None:\\n    import matplotlib\\n    matplotlib.use(\\\"Agg\\\")\\n    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n    cov = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"ledger_6_1.csv\\\"))\\n    gnp = read_csv(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"ledger_gnp.csv\\\"))\\n    # palette: reference categorical slots 1, 2, 3, 4 and text-primary for pw (validated, see run.log)\\n    rungs_cov = [(\\\"old_lt001\\\", \\\"old pair floor\\\", \\\"#2a78d6\\\"), (\\\"xpair_lt001\\\", \\\"exact-size pair floor\\\", \\\"#eb6834\\\"),\\n                 (\\\"best_lt001\\\", \\\"best count (closed / flip)\\\", \\\"#1baf7a\\\"), (\\\"harper\\\", \\\"Harper (capped)\\\", \\\"#eda100\\\"), (\\\"pw\\\", \\\"pathwidth\\\", \\\"#0b0b0b\\\")]\\n    rungs_gnp = [(\\\"old_lt001\\\", \\\"old pair floor\\\", \\\"#2a78d6\\\"), (\\\"xpair_lt001\\\", \\\"exact-size pair floor\\\", \\\"#eb6834\\\"),\\n                 (\\\"best_lt001\\\", \\\"best count (separator / closed)\\\", \\\"#1baf7a\\\"), (\\\"harper\\\", \\\"Harper (capped)\\\", \\\"#eda100\\\"), (\\\"pw\\\", \\\"pathwidth\\\", \\\"#0b0b0b\\\")]\\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(10.5, 4.4), sharey=True)\\n    for ax, rows, rungs, title in ((axes[0], cov, rungs_cov, \\\"random clique covers (6, 1), m = n, certified\\\"),\\n                                   (axes[1], gnp, rungs_gnp, \\\"G(n, 10/n), pilot graphs, proved\\\")):\\n        ns = sorted({int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) for r in rows})\\n        for i, n in enumerate(ns):\\n            g = [r for r in rows if int(r[\\\"n\\\"]) == n]\\n            pw = np.array([int(r[\\\"pw\\\"]) for r in g])\\n            meds = []\\n            for key, lab, col in rungs:\\n                gap = pw - np.array([int(r[key]) for r in g])\\n                meds.append(float(np.median(gap)))\\n            ax.plot([n, n], [max(meds), min(meds)], color=\\\"#c3c2b7\\\", linewidth=1.5, zorder=1)\\n            for (key, lab, col), m in zip(rungs, meds):\\n                ax.plot([n], [m], \\\"o\\\", color=col, markersize=8, markeredgecolor=\\\"#fcfcfb\\\", markeredgewidth=1.2, zorder=3,\\n                        label=lab if i == 0 else None)\\n                if i == len(ns) - 1:\\n                    ax.annotate(lab, (n, m), xytext=(8, 0), textcoords=\\\"offset points\\\", fontsize=8, color=\\\"#52514e\\\", va=\\\"center\\\")\\n        ax.set_xlabel(\\\"n\\\")\\n        ax.set_title(title, fontsize=9, color=\\\"#52514e\\\", loc=\\\"left\\\")\\n        ax.set_xticks(ns)\\n        ax.set_xlim(min(ns) - 3, max(ns) + 22)\\n        ax.grid(axis=\\\"y\\\", color=\\\"#e8e7e3\\\", linewidth=0.8)\\n        for s in (\\\"top\\\", \\\"right\\\"):\\n            ax.spines[s].set_visible(False)\\n        ax.spines[\\\"left\\\"].set_color(\\\"#c3c2b7\\\")\\n        ax.spines[\\\"bottom\\\"].set_color(\\\"#c3c2b7\\\")\\n    axes[0].set_ylabel(\\\"stacks below the pathwidth (median per n)\\\")\\n    axes[0].invert_yaxis()\\n    axes[0].legend(loc=\\\"lower left\\\", fontsize=8, frameon=False)\\n    fig.tight_layout()\\n    fig.savefig(os.path.join(HERE, \\\"ladder.png\\\"), dpi=160)\\n    log(\\\"draw: ladder.png\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef main() -> None:\\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--stage\\\", default=\\\"all\\\", choices=[\\\"all\\\", \\\"covers\\\", \\\"gnp\\\", \\\"stats\\\", \\\"draw\\\"])\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--workers\\\", type=int, default=6)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--max-t\\\", type=int, default=16)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--budget\\\", type=float, default=60.0)\\n    a = ap.parse_args()\\n    if a.stage in (\\\"all\\\", \\\"covers\\\"):\\n        stage_covers(a.workers)\\n    if a.stage in (\\\"all\\\", \\\"gnp\\\"):\\n        stage_gnp(a.workers, a.max_t, a.budget)\\n    if a.stage in (\\\"all\\\", \\\"stats\\\"):\\n        stage_stats()\\n    if a.stage in (\\\"all\\\", \\\"draw\\\"):\\n        stage_draw()\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\nEOF\\nuptime; rm -f reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger/run.log; nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger/run.py --stage covers --workers 6 2>&1 | tail -5\",\"description\":\"Write the ledger script and run the covers stage\",\"timeout\":600000}},\"wire_ingest_context\":{\"toolu_01AfUfM8SNXHdwJV5R5JBATC\":{\"cwd\":\"/home/al/dev/MOSP\"}}}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_started\",\"task_id\":\"b7n8c7ztk\",\"run_id\":\"0mvycyszu-7ee42177\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01AfUfM8SNXHdwJV5R5JBATC\",\"description\":\"Write the ledger script and run the covers stage\",\"is_backgrounded\":false,\"task_type\":\"local_bash\",\"uuid\":\"c61a6c2d-93dc-4bbf-a092-7f3992e8eb36\",\"session_id\":\"c821cc2c-f627-4785-bc52-942e492e87f6\"}","+{\"type\":\"tool_progress\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01AfUfM8SNXHdwJV5R5JBATC-heartbeat-0\",\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01AfUfM8SNXHdwJV5R5JBATC\",\"elapsed_time_seconds\":30,\"heartbeat\":true,\"session_id\":\"c821cc2c-f627-4785-bc52-942e492e87f6\",\"uuid\":\"893ea3ff-537f-4e60-99f9-eb25226fd978\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_notification\",\"task_