″, B;     `β*(c)`; the finite form against the pilot, §5) and     `reports/scratch/clique_cover_moment/README.md` + `REPORT_generator.md`     (the clique-cover version; `β*(d, μ)`; the threshold at excess 1; the     fitted generator).   - `reports/random_graph_pathwidth_survey.md` §1 and §7(d) (what is     published; the pilot's fitted slopes).   - The Lean headers: `lean/MOSPFormalization/EmptyPair.lean`     (`exists_empty_pair_of_layout`, `exists_closedNbhd_card_le`,     `exists_empty_pair`), `FirstMoment.lean` (`IsEmptyPair`, `gnpWeight`,     `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le`), `FirstMomentAsymptotics.lean`,     `CliqueCoverMoment.lean` (`coverGraph`, `avoidCount`,     `prob_coversOfMospValueLe_le`), `ForestCover.lean` (the layer lemma;     `isEmptyPair_coverGraph_of_subset`). - **The object.** A layout of vertex separation `≤ k` gives, at the prefix   of size `t = ⌈(n − k)/2⌉`, a separator `S` (the active suffix, `≤ k`   vertices) with the prefix `A` and the inactive suffix `R` on either side   and no `A–R` edge. Padding `S` to exactly `k` vertices from `R`:   `|A| = t`, `|R| = N − t`, `|S| = k`, `N = n − k`, `A ∪ R ∪ S = V`. The pair   count on record sums over `(A, R)`; this loop sums over `S` with the inner   probability `P(G − S` has a balanced empty bipartition`)` computed from   the component structure, and over two further representatives: the   *closed* pair (`S = N(A) ∩ N(R)`) and the weighted count   `Y = Σ_P 1[P empty] / Z(P)` for any `Z ≤ X`. Say exactly which event is   counted in every statement; the three are not the same event, and the   relaxation \"no component larger than `t`\" is weaker than the bipartition   event (plan §0, correction 3). - **Nothing is solved twice.** The pilot graphs   (`reports/scratch/gnp_pilot/results.csv`: 6,542 proved with layouts,   `n = 20–120`), the certified ensembles (`learning/data/ensemble/results*.csv`,   regenerate from seed with `learning.ensemble.generate(Cell.parse(...), index)`)   and the corpus (`solutions/`, read only) carry exact values already. New   exact solves are allowed only where an item says so: tiny graphs that are   not MOSP instances (`n ≤ 24`), by the subset DP   (`learning.first_moment.vertex_separation_brute`, `n ≤ 16`) or the C   program `pathwidth_solver/cli/pathwidth` (graph6 on stdin, `-l` for the   layout), never the Python pathwidth solver; every layout persisted in the   item's CSV under `reports/scratch/separator_moment/`; never   `solutions_dir=None`; never `solutions/`. - **State before you prove, and check before you state.** Every statement   that will be called a lemma or theorem — on paper or in Lean — is first   checked by brute force on small instances (every graph to 9 vertices by   `nauty-geng`, as `reports/scratch/empty_pair/check.py` does; every   labelled graph to 7 for weighted counts, as   `reports/scratch/first_moment/check.py` does), and the check's script and   log are kept. Two earlier `sorry`s in this development hid false   statements, not hard ones. - **A measurement is not a theorem; a first moment is not the constant; a   fit is not a rate.** Every number carries its size range and its   regenerate command. Where a rate is fitted from finite `N`, say \"fitted\".   Every item ends with \"what this does not claim\". Say \"we found no prior   statement\", never \"first\". The planner's estimates in the plan are   predictions to be tested, never results to be cited. - **Nats per vertex, with the conversion beside them**: the pair exponent's   slope at `β*` is `3.3–3.4` per unit of `β` on `G(n, c/n)` at `c = 6–10`   (compute it for each cell you quote), so a gain of `g` nats per vertex is   `g / 3.3` in `β`. Report both.  ## Compute, and the machine - 32 cores, shared with the owner's other projects; the load is often above   24 from work that is not ours. Every process under `nice -n 19`; at most   8 workers, 4 if the one-minute load in `uptime` is above 24. Check   `uptime` before anything parallel. Find processes by 