and the split is not the instances'. The counts' floors are\nmodel statements evaluated at the instance's sizes, not instance\nstatements; a `< 1` floor above `pw` is not a violation. No rate is\nfitted here; \"grows with `n`\" is read off six (four) sizes. The medians\nare of 50–150 instances per size.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np=\"Ralph_Loops/loop0011/iterations.md\"; s=open(p).read()\nold=\"- [ ] **11 The slack ledger\"; assert old in s\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s.replace(old,\"- [x] **11 The slack ledger\"))\nEOF\ngrep -n \"^- \\[\" Ralph_Loops/loop0011/iterations.md | sed -n 9,14p; tail -5 reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger/gate.log","description":"Append §11 to the report, mark item 11 done, check gate progress"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01RoRi9DCT1nDwkxCDhE9gmS":{"cwd":"/home/al/dev/MOSP"}}}
